title: Judiciary Reform
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "SPD" and judiciary_timer = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; judiciary_timer += 6
card-image: img/portraits/RadbruchGustav.jpg
tags: govt_affairs

= Judiciary Reform

The Judiciary is one of the most reactionary components of the government, along with the military. Many jurists have held office since the days of the Emperor. They give violent fascists like Adolf Hitler laughably light sentences, while ruthlessly persecuting leftists and pacifists for lesser crimes.

[? if judicial_reform <= 0 : There is great demand in our membership for reforming the judiciary, although this may bring us into a collision course with our coalition allies. ?]
[? if judicial_reform == 1 : We have started on the path to judicial reform. While some of the most antideluvian and biased justices have been replaced, many still remain. More should be done. ?]
[? if judicial_reform == 2 : We have successfully reformed the judiciary, to some extent. At the very least, the courts will not actively obstruct our attempts to prosecute crimes committed by the far-right. ?]
[? if judicial_reform >= 5 : We have exhaustively reformed the judiciary. The courts have been stacked with sympathetic justices who will turn a blind eye to our own excesses while aggressively prosecuting crimes committed by the far-right. ?]

- @reform: Carry out substantial judicial reforms,
- @recruitment_campaign: Increase training funding to incentivise greater training of younger judges.
- @retirement_age: Institute a mandatory judicial retirement age of 70
- @retirement_age_2: Lower the mandatory retirement age to 65
- @elected_judges: Introduce popular elections for judges
- @as_is: Leave the judiciary as it is.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@elected_judges
view-if: elected_judges == 0
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 2 if in_grand_coalition == 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_weimar_coalition == 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_social_christian_coalition == 1; elected_judges = 1; judicial_reform = (((pro_republic + socialism) - nationalism)/20); democratization += ((pro_republic - nationalism)/10); coup_progress += 2

We introduce popular election for judges, which will hopefully disrupt the reactionary establishment's hold on the judicial system. [? if nationalism > pro_republic && nationalism > socialism : The prevalence of Nationalism means this measure is likely to backfire, however. ?] 

@recruitment_campaign
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget.
view-if: judicial_reform <= 3
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; judicial_reform += 1; democratisation += 3; pro_republic += 2;

We introduce greater funding for judicial training, helping more young judges enter the system. [? if in_grand_coalition : Our Coalition partners are not convinced by this, but are satisfied with the lack of action against existing judges. ?]

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget.
view-if: judicial_reform <= 3
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: judicial_vote = 1
go-to: judiciary_done if not legislature_enabled; legislative_menu if legislature_enabled

We propose a bill to perform substantial reforms in the judiciary.

@judiciary_done
on-arrival: budget -= 1; democratization += 2; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition == 1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 2; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); coup_progress += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if historical_mode

We investigate jurists who have shown themselves to have biased or corrupt behavior, and try to remove them, replacing them with more democratically-oriented jurists. This obviously raises quite a great deal of ire in conservative circles, including within our coalition. 

@retirement_age
view-if: retirement_age == 0
on-arrival: retirement_age = 1; democratization += 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 1; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); judiciary_timer += 6; coup_progress += 1

We institute a mandatory retirement age, immediately filtering out some of the oldest and most reactionary judges, while leaving most of the system intact. It will be slow, but it is a step in our work reforming the judiciary.

@retirement_age_2
view-if: retirement_age == 1
on-arrival: retirement_age = 2; democratization += 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 1; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); judiciary_timer += 6; coup_progress += 1

We lower the mandatory retirement age, immediately filtering out some of the oldest and most reactionary judges, while leaving most of the system intact. It will be slow, but it is a step in our work reforming the judiciary.

@as_is
go-to: root
